& [Profiles]
  + change_set is cantor-sjs-repository-change-set/0.1
  + diff_inventory is cantor-sjs-diff-inventory/0.1
  + element_event is cantor-sjs-element-history-event/0.1
  + verification_receipt is cantor-sjs-repository-graph-verification/0.1

& [Requirements]
  + [CSG-001] strict profiles closed enums deny_unknown_fields and bounded machine forms are exact
  + [CSG-002] repository change-set turn conversation node edge event and commit identities use strict grammars and uniqueness
  + [CSG-003] stable element IDs are semantic identities independent of mutable line numbers and ordinary path movement
  + [CSG-004] repository paths are normalized relative forward-slash paths with traversal root drive backslash NUL empty and duplicate refusal
  + [CSG-005] DiffInventory independently binds repository branch predecessor ordered changed paths identities and self-excluding digest
  + [CSG-006] Added Modified Deleted Renamed and GeneratedRefresh entries enforce exact old/new path and before/after identity shapes
  + [CSG-007] graph nodes use the closed Pinky node-kind vocabulary unique IDs bounded content refs and exact optional path/digest coupling
  + [CSG-008] graph edges use the closed Pinky edge-kind vocabulary unique IDs existing distinct endpoints and no duplicate kind/source/target triple
  + [CSG-009] each ElementHistoryEvent binds one stable element one operation one turn one change set reason refs identity transition coverage nonclaims frontier and self-excluding digest
  + [CSG-010] one change set refuses duplicate event UUID duplicate element ID and conflicting event coverage
  + [CSG-011] event operations are compatible with every covered independent diff entry including tombstone deletion and identity-preserving rename
  + [CSG-012] every inventory coordinate is covered by at least one event and every event coordinate resolves to the inventory
  + [CSG-013] GeneratedRefresh inventory is covered by generated-refresh events only with source and justification refs and complete enumerated paths
  + [CSG-014] event typed ref sets resolve to graph nodes of the required kinds and each event node modifies an element node
  + [CSG-015] foreign exclusions are normalized unique and disjoint from inventory paths event paths and content-bearing graph paths
  + [CSG-016] change-set inventory digest repository predecessor and branch must exactly join the independent DiffInventory
  + [CSG-017] verification emits deterministic counts complete coverage verification_only authority physical_contact false nonauthority and self-excluding digest
  + [CSG-018] result replay unknown-field tamper digest drift dangling refs duplicate graph path traversal missing coverage foreign overlap and resource overflow are refused
  + [CSG-019] a read-only CLI accepts exact change-set and diff-inventory JSON paths emits the receipt to stdout or an optional output file and performs no Git process network provider or mutation action
  + [CSG-020] unit integration CLI evidence format Clippy attribution and exact workspace gates bind implementation without new Cargo dependency

& [Constraints]
  + [C01] one safe Rust module and one cantor_ecosystem lib export
  + [C02] one file-input verification binary in the existing crate
  + [C03] current dependencies only and zero Cargo manifest or lock delta
  + [C04] maximum change-set machine form 1048576 bytes
  + [C05] maximum diff-inventory machine form 524288 bytes
  + [C06] maximum 1024 diff entries 1024 nodes 4096 edges 1024 events and 1024 foreign exclusions
  + [C07] maximum 128 refs or coverage coordinates per event
  + [C08] maximum path 1024 bytes semantic ID 256 bytes reason or text 4096 bytes
  + [C09] UUID is lowercase canonical 8-4-4-4-12 hexadecimal text
  + [C10] SHA256 is uppercase sixty-four hexadecimal text and commit is lowercase forty hexadecimal text
  + [C11] branch is refs/heads plus normalized ref text
  + [C12] repository ID semantic IDs node IDs and edge IDs use bounded lowercase semantic-token grammar
  + [C13] canonical JSON is serde declaration order compact encoding with domain-separated SHA256
  + [C14] digest computation clears only the subject digest field
  + [C15] graph node and edge vocabularies exactly match signed Pinky contract
  + [C16] event reference type agreement is mechanically validated
  + [C17] no filesystem access exists in the library module
  + [C18] CLI filesystem reads and optional output write are the only physical operations
  + [C19] CLI creates an output parent only when a nonempty parent exists and never invokes Git
  + [C20] no unsafe platform environment clock randomness process network provider model MCP persistence commit push activation FPGA or Minecraft surface
  + [C21] all owned artifacts receive per-element change-set history before commit while foreign paths remain excluded
  + [C22] physical Git inventory acquisition and hook enforcement require separate authority

